<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47838" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tĕrē^bra</span></b> , ae,
			f. (<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>neutr.</i> collat. form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tĕ-rē^brum</span></b> ,
				<i><span class="en">Hier. in Isa. 12, 44, 12 al.</span></i>)
			[tero]. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>An instrument for boring</i>, <i>a
				borer</i>, <i>an auger</i>, <i>gimlet</i>, <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 41, 3</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Col. 4, 29, 15 sq.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 7, 56,
				57, § 198</span></i>; <i><span class="en">17, 15, 25, §
			116</span></i>; <i><span class="en">37, 13, 76,
				§ 200</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> As a surgical 
			 instrument, <i>a trephine</i>, <i><span class="en">Cels. 8,
			3</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A military engine for boring through walls in
			sieges</i>, <i><span class="en">Vitr. 10, 13, 7</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
